{
  "id": "minimax-h3-singularity-v2-pack",
  "name": "Community — MiniMax H3 (Singularity v2)",
  "version": "1.0.2",
  "author": "WarmBloodAban (AIGC-Singularity)",
  "nsfw": false,
  "minComfyuiVersion": "v0.34.0",
  "description": "WarmBloodAban's Singularity v2 (released 2026-10-23), the second version of the HDR merge-and-finetune of MiniMax H3 ref2va, as the pruned int8 build: the same 21 GB size, graphs and 20-step recipe as the v1.3 checkpoint in the Singularity pack, and one checkpoint for text, image and reference to video. The v1.3 pack is unchanged, so both looks stay available: v1.3 is the calmer one, v2 the one that moves. MEASURED 2026-10-25 on a 12 GB RTX 4070 Ti (SimpliGen engine 0.42.0, 864x480, 5 s, 20 steps, text to video, three prompts x three seeds, the same seeds on v2 and v1.3): v2 fixes v1.3's weak spot, motion. Optical flow per frame rose 38% on a tracking cyclist shot (7.7 vs 5.6, level with H3 Midnight) and 22% in a sword duel (3.0 vs 2.5, more than Midnight), on every seed, and v2 was the only model whose duellists actually crossed blades. The trade: it is darker still. A dim-studio portrait came back at half v1.3's brightness (mean luma 17 vs 35) and a sunlit courtyard at two thirds (56 vs 82), on every seed, and v2 frames tighter on every prompt. Close-up faces stay as crisp as v1.3's. Same speed as v1.3: about 200 s per five-second 480p shot at 20 steps on the bare graph, about 2 minutes in the app with faster attention and Spectrum on (all three cards checked in the app 2026-10-25). The author recommends naming the style in the prompt (photorealistic, East Asian realism, 3D CG, cinematic CG) and keeping prompts under about 5,000 characters. LICENCE: the model card says Apache-2.0, but this is a derivative of MiniMax H3 weights, which places it under the MiniMax H3 Community License like every other H3 checkpoint - check that licence before shipping anything made with it. Encoder and VAEs are the official Comfy-Org files shared with the other H3 packs, so the only new download is the 21 GB checkpoint.",
  "tags": [
    "Local",
    "Video",
    "T2V",
    "I2V",
    "R2V",
    "MiniMax H3",
    "Finetune",
    "HDR",
    "Singularity",
    "v2"
  ],
