      "description": "Reference to video on Singularity v2 through the same graph as the Singularity pack. CHECKED IN THE APP 2026-10-25 (480p, 5 s, about 2 min each): one picture of a woman held her face through a walking shot on three seeds, each hitting the prompted glance and smile; a two-person shot from two separate pictures held both people and spoke its one line word for word, with no extra words after it. The author's v2 notes add a fix for audio-reference conditioning (not measured here). The numbers below are from text to video. MEASURED 2026-10-25 on a 12 GB RTX 4070 Ti (SimpliGen engine 0.42.0, 864x480, 5 s, 20 steps, text to video, three prompts x three seeds, the same seeds on v2 and v1.3): v2 fixes v1.3's weak spot, motion. Optical flow per frame rose 38% on a tracking cyclist shot (7.7 vs 5.6, level with H3 Midnight) and 22% in a sword duel (3.0 vs 2.5, more than Midnight), on every seed, and v2 was the only model whose duellists actually crossed blades. The trade: it is darker still. A dim-studio portrait came back at half v1.3's brightness (mean luma 17 vs 35) and a sunlit courtyard at two thirds (56 vs 82), on every seed, and v2 frames tighter on every prompt. Close-up faces stay as crisp as v1.3's. Same speed as v1.3: about 200 s per five-second 480p shot at 20 steps on the bare graph, about 2 minutes in the app with faster attention and Spectrum on (all three cards checked in the app 2026-10-25). LICENCE: the model card says Apache-2.0, but this is a derivative of MiniMax H3 weights, which places it under the MiniMax H3 Community License like every other H3 checkpoint - check that licence before shipping anything made with it.",
